course: dictionary
lesson: 4750
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word host is a good example. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is the context, and ask which meaning fits.
explain: «When invited to a party, reply by the date asked so the host knows how many children are coming.» Here the host is the person who invites the guests and looks after them, because the guests reply to the host.
explain: «At a sleepover the house rules belong to the host's parents, including bedtime.» Here host means the family whose home the children stay in. Test your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the word.
explain: Host can also be a verb, which means to hold an event or have guests. A country can host the Olympics, and a family can host a refugee. A flea lives on a dog, so the dog is its host.
fact: A host is a person who invites guests and looks after them, for example at a party.
fact: A host can also be a person who presents a TV or radio show.
fact: A host can be an animal or plant that a parasite lives on, like a dog for a flea.
fact: To host means to hold an event or have guests, and a host of things means a lot of them.
fact: «qǐng jìn» means come in, please, and it is said by the host at the door.
exercise: «When invited to a party, reply by the date asked so the host knows how many children are coming.» Who is the host here? | The dog that barks at the door | The guest who is coming to the party | The cake that is served at the party | *The person who invited the guests
exercise: In science, a flea lives on a host like a dog. What is the host in this sentence? | A person who presents a TV show | A party guest who arrives late | *An animal or plant that a parasite lives on
exercise: «qǐng jìn» is said by the host at the door. What does it mean? | Wait here, please | Go out | *Come in, please | Goodbye and thank you
test: «The UK's Homes for Ukraine scheme let local families host them.» Here host means | A TV show presenter | To leave early | A computer that runs a website | *To give a home to and look after
test: «A host of things» means | *A lot of things | Only one thing | A small drink | A shop that sells food
exam: What is the best way to find the meaning of host in «a fair host evens it out»? | Skip the word and never read it again | *Put each meaning into the sentence and see which one makes sense | Guess the first meaning you think of | Count the letters in the word
